381 0 obj
<<
/Title (Telecom strategy does not exist in a vacuum. Equipment shortages, spectrum auction prices, and global supply chain disruptions can also cause operational bottlenecks. Corporate strategy works alongside government regulations \(TRAI\) and supply-side measures.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 372 0 R
/Prev 392 0 R
>>
endobj
382 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Telecom Regulatory Authority of India \(TRAI\) acts as the central regulator, similar to how the RBI manages monetary policy. It manages fair competition, regulates interconnection usage charges \(IUC\), and supports the stability of the digital payment ecosystem built on top of telecom networks.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 373 0 R
/Next 383 0 R
>>
endobj
383 0 obj
<<
/Title (Decisions regarding spectrum pricing and tariff caps are made within a legal framework. While companies like Jio and Airtel have the freedom to set retail prices, TRAI monitors these to prevent monopolistic predatory pricing or illegal cartels. The framework ensures that inflation in digital services does not disrupt economic growth.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 373 0 R
/Prev 382 0 R
>>
endobj
